  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Mandelic acid is an antibacterial used, for example, as a urinary antiseptic and in irrigating solutions. It is an approved drug, though not an EMA-authorised medicine, and is used only to a limited extent.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q412293&quot;>Wikidata Q412293</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>mandelic acid</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>B05CA06, J01XX06</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13218&quot;>DB13218</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:35825&quot;>35825</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q412293&quot;>Q412293</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C8H8O3</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>152.149 g/mol (Drugs.Common (25.09))</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
